//// The errors of the operating system that a connection can meet, by the
//// names that OTP gives them.

import gleam/dynamic.{type Dynamic}

/// An error of the OS, by the name that OTP gives it. The variants are the
/// names that OTP 28 (`erl_posix_str.c`) and OTP 29 (`erl_errno_str.c`) give
/// an errno on Linux, macOS, the BSDs, Solaris and Windows: each variant is
/// the atom of OTP, for example `Econnrefused` for `econnrefused` and
/// `ENoMore` for `e_no_more`. OTP 29 gives a name that is in neither list
/// (from the C library, or `errno_N` for an errno with no name): that name
/// is `Unlisted(name)`, so no error is lost.
